WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.729
A bedside scan that takes about two and a half minutes and answers one question.

00:00:08.879 --> 00:00:11.377
Is this stomach empty?

00:00:13.027 --> 00:00:16.591
A fasting history is not always reliable.

00:00:16.741 --> 00:00:25.169
Of 538 fasted elective patients, 6.2% had a full stomach on ultrasound.

00:00:25.319 --> 00:00:31.912
In another study, a full stomach was found in 56% of emergency cases.

00:00:33.562 --> 00:00:38.491
Adults: curved low-frequency probe (1 to 5 MHz), abdominal preset.

00:00:38.641 --> 00:00:45.277
Children under 40 kg: linear high-frequency probe (5 to 12 MHz).

00:00:45.427 --> 00:00:48.927
Start supine or semi-recumbent.

00:00:50.577 --> 00:00:55.741
Epigastrium, just below the xiphisternum, sagittal plane.

00:00:55.891 --> 00:01:00.095
Perpendicular to the skin, marker towards the head.

00:01:00.245 --> 00:01:03.724
Sweep across from the left costal margin.

00:01:05.374 --> 00:01:07.551
Find the antrum.

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:12.289
Left lobe of the liver: its lower edge.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:16.942
The antrum, in cross-section.

00:01:17.092 --> 00:01:19.739
Behind it, the pancreas.

00:01:19.889 --> 00:01:25.117
Deeper: the aorta in long axis, in front of the spine.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:29.193
Standard plane: the antrum at the level of the aorta.

00:01:30.843 --> 00:01:33.810
Turn the patient onto the right side.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:39.977
Gravity moves the contents to the antrum: the more sensitive view.

00:01:40.127 --> 00:01:44.374
Only call a stomach empty after looking in this position.

00:01:44.524 --> 00:01:49.666
If turning is not practical: semi-recumbent.

00:01:51.316 --> 00:01:57.739
Empty: small, flat, thick-walled. The bull’s eye.

00:01:57.889 --> 00:02:05.762
Clear fluid: round, thin-walled, dark inside. Air bubbles give a starry night.

00:02:05.912 --> 00:02:09.049
Thick fluid, such as milk: uniformly bright.

00:02:09.199 --> 00:02:15.089
Solid, early: frosted glass that hides the deeper structures.

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:20.915
Solid, later: mixed bright content in a distended antrum.

00:02:22.565 --> 00:02:25.745
When the content is clear fluid, grade it.

00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:28.862
Grade 0: empty in both positions.

00:02:29.012 --> 00:02:34.090
Grade 1: fluid only in the right lateral position. Low volume.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:41.111
Grade 2: fluid in both positions. Likely 1.5 mL/kg or more.

00:02:42.761 --> 00:02:50.122
Freeze in the right lateral position, between contractions.

00:02:50.272 --> 00:02:55.116
Trace the serosa all the way round. Mean of three readings.

00:02:55.266 --> 00:03:03.865
Volume (mL) = 27 + 14.6 × area (cm²) − 1.28 × age (years).

00:03:05.515 --> 00:03:12.620
Empty, or clear fluid below 1.5 mL/kg: consistent with a fasted stomach.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:19.300
Clear fluid at or above 1.5 mL/kg, or any thick fluid or solid: full stomach.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:24.571
The scan informs the plan. You decide with the whole patient in mind.

00:03:26.221 --> 00:03:29.230
How many scans does it take to learn?

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:39.110
About 33 supervised examinations for a 95% success rate (Arzola 2013).

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.906
Start counting.
